**2. Register in `Program.cs`:**

```csharp
var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);

// Add Problem Details support + custom handler
builder.Services.AddProblemDetails();
builder.Services.AddExceptionHandler<GlobalExceptionHandler>();

var app = builder.Build();

// Must be early in the pipeline
app.UseExceptionHandler();

// Your endpoints...
app.MapGet("/example/{id}", (int id) =>
{
    throw new KeyNotFoundException($"Item {id} not found");
});

app.Run();
```

**How it works:**

- `AddExceptionHandler<T>()` registers your `IExceptionHandler` (.NET 8+)
- `UseExceptionHandler()` catches all unhandled exceptions globally
- The switch expression maps exception types → status codes
- 500 errors suppress `exception.Message` to avoid leaking internals
- Response automatically gets `application/problem+json` content type

No try-catch needed in any endpoint — the middleware handles everything centrally.
